From d31524fe5187724f41749ece70a4b470a369240d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:21:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(engine): bind the resolution-pick keyword anaphor to
 the exiled tracked set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Exile a card from your hand with a number of time counters on it equal to
its mana value. If it doesn't have suspend, it gains suspend." (The
Eleventh Doctor, Amy's Home) strict-failed to `Effect::Unimplemented`
because the pick is an untargeted choice made while the ability resolves
(CR 608.2d): it reaches neither the grant condition's subject nor
`ResolvedAbility.targets`, so the gate could only fall through to its
`TriggeringSource` fallback — the Doctor itself.

Both halves of the clause are now re-anchored onto the tracked set the pick
publishes, with the keyword test folded into the set selector:
`TrackedSetFiltered { filter: <no suspend>, caused_by: Exiled }`. That is
Forge's `Card.IsRemembered+withoutSuspend` composition expressed with this
engine's existing parts, and it expresses "the cards exiled this way that
don't have suspend" as ONE per-member selector, so no separate condition is
left to misbind and no printed `Suspend N—{cost}` can be clobbered to {0}.

Three seams had to carry that shape:

  * `publish_effect_zone_choice_tracked_set` stamps the producer action.
    An INTERACTIVE exile publishes through the choice-completion seam, not
    through `publish_tracked_set_for_resolution`'s event-derived arm, so
    nothing wrote `tracked_set_member_causes` and a `caused_by: Exiled`
    selector matched nothing. The cause is derived from the destination
    through the same `this_way_cause_for_zone` authority the completion
    seam already stamps `EffectResolutionResult.cause` with.
  * `GenericEffect`'s broadcast arm enumerates a tracked-set filter's
    members. It scanned only the battlefield, so a set of exiled cards was
    unreachable however it was selected.
  * Entry counters split by answerability. `enter_with_counters` was
    resolved at resolver entry with `recipient: None`, so an
    `ObjectScope::Recipient` count walked its fallback ladder down to the
    ability SOURCE and stamped the SOURCE's mana value — the chosen MV-3
    card entered exile with 0 time counters. Counts that do not read the
    moved object stay eagerly resolved; only those that do are carried as
    `EnterCounterSpec::PerObject` and answered per object by
    `enter_with_counters_for_object`.

Measured: the chosen card enters exile with 3 time counters and gains
suspend; a card with printed `Suspend 4—{U}` keeps its parameters. The
other three binding classes (declared stack target, injected target,
trigger source) are pinned unchanged.

23218 engine unit tests pass (`game::casting::tests::witherbloom_…` fails
on this fork's 362-card WHO pool and predates this change), 103
`effects::change_zone`, 2706 `effects::` + `engine_resolution_choices::`,
and 13 `keyword_anaphor_subject_binding` integration tests.
